 "stimulus_html": "<figure id=\"fig9_12\">\n<img src=\"exercises/media/f2996e12beabca3b.png\" alt=\"On the left is a Chinese man sitting on the ground with his head in his hands. Behind him is a wall covered in writing, some of which reads “Importation of Chinese barbarians into the country must be stopped by the ballot or bullet; vicious, immoral, heathenish; degraded labor of Asia; John Chinaman is an idolater and heathen.” On the right, men holding knives, stones, and guns come towards the man. A woman, Columbia, stands between them. The caption at the bottom of the cartoon reads Columbia says “Hands off, gentlemen! America means fair play for all men!”\">\n<figcaption>Within the image in this political cartoon from 1871 are such terms as “Coolie, Slave, Pauper, and Rat-Eater…The Chinaman works cheap because he is a Barbarian…” Underneath the image is this text: “The Chinese Question. Columbia: ‘Hands off gentlemen! America means fair play for all men!’”</figcaption>\n</figure>\n<p><i>Refer to the image provided.</i></p>\n",
